**Class:** `Country`  (collection `Country`, database `orbit-geo`)

**Why:** `Country` is static reference/lookup data read on many page loads (dropdowns / pick-lists). On Cosmos every read is metered as RU — uncached reference reads drove `orbit-geo` to ~28k RU during testing. On the old VM MongoDB these were absorbed for free from the RAM working set.

Part of the **Database Structure Effort** (MongoDB → CosmosDB migration).

---

## Recommended implementation — pick ONE scheme

Both wrap `Country`'s existing `FetchActive()` / `FetchAll()` read and invalidate on `Save()`. Cache key per scheme: `Country.Active` (add a `Country.All` key too if both reads are used).

### Option A — .NET `IMemoryCache` (in-process)  ⟵ recommended for this data

```csharp
// In Country — wrap the existing read in the cache:
public static List<Country> FetchActive( )
{
    return ReferenceCache.GetOrAdd( "Country.Active", ( ) =>
        /* ...the EXISTING FetchActive() body, e.g.:
           GetCollection( )
               .Find( Builders<Country>.Filter.Eq( t => t.IsActive, true ) )
               .SortBy( t => t.Name )
               .ToList( ) */ );
}

// In Country.Save( ), after base.Save( ), so admin edits refresh the cache:
ReferenceCache.Invalidate( "Country.Active" );
```

**Shared helper (implement once for the whole effort):**

```csharp
// ORBIT.Model/Helper/ReferenceCache.cs  — implement ONCE for the whole effort.
using Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.Memory;

namespace ORBIT.Model.Helper
{
    public static class ReferenceCache
    {
        private static readonly IMemoryCache _cache =
            new MemoryCache( new MemoryCacheOptions( ) );
        private static readonly TimeSpan DefaultTtl = TimeSpan.FromHours( 4 );

        public static T GetOrAdd<T>( String key, Func<T> factory )
        {
            return _cache.GetOrCreate( key, entry =>
            {
                entry.AbsoluteExpirationRelativeToNow = DefaultTtl;
                return factory( );
            } );
        }

        public static void Invalidate( String key ) => _cache.Remove( key );
    }
}
```

### Option B — Redis (distributed, shared across instances)

```csharp
// Same call site, distributed cache instead (shared across App Service instances):
public static List<Country> FetchActive( )
{
    return RedisCache.GetOrAdd( "Country.Active", ( ) =>
        /* ...the EXISTING FetchActive() body (same as above)... */ );
}

// In Country.Save( ), after base.Save( ):
RedisCache.Invalidate( "Country.Active" );
```

**Shared helper (implement once):**

```csharp
// ORBIT.Model/Helper/RedisCache.cs  — implement ONCE. Call RedisCache.Initialize(mux)
// at startup with the app's existing StackExchange.Redis multiplexer.
using System.Text.Json;
using StackExchange.Redis;

namespace ORBIT.Model.Helper
{
    public static class RedisCache
    {
        private static IConnectionMultiplexer _mux;
        public static void Initialize( IConnectionMultiplexer mux ) => _mux = mux;
        private static readonly TimeSpan DefaultTtl = TimeSpan.FromHours( 4 );

        public static T GetOrAdd<T>( String key, Func<T> factory, TimeSpan? ttl = null )
        {
            IDatabase db = _mux?.GetDatabase( );
            if ( db == null ) return factory( );          // not configured -> source
            try
            {
                RedisValue cached = db.StringGet( key );
                if ( cached.HasValue ) return JsonSerializer.Deserialize<T>( cached! );
            }
            catch { return factory( ); }                  // Redis hiccup -> source
            T value = factory( );
            try { db.StringSet( key, JsonSerializer.Serialize( value ), ttl ?? DefaultTtl ); }
            catch { /* best-effort cache write */ }
            return value;
        }

        public static void Invalidate( String key )
        {
            try { _mux?.GetDatabase( ).KeyDelete( key ); }
            catch { /* best-effort */ }
        }
    }
}
```

---

**Recommendation:** `IMemoryCache` (Option A) for this reference/lookup data — it's tiny, static, and cheap to re-fetch per instance, so per-instance copies are fine and avoid a network hop. Choose Redis (Option B) only if you need **instant cross-instance invalidation** on admin edits. Same call-site API, so switching is a one-word change (`ReferenceCache` ⟷ `RedisCache`).

